=======================================================================
   EMC - BACKUP GUIDE
=======================================================================

Use the backup_emc.sh and restore_emc.sh script for backup and restore.

Use remove_emc.sh to remove EMC and dependancies from your system.

Call backup_emc.sh with the -i option to CREATE an INSTALL archive
or with the -b option to CREATE a BACKUP archive

The archives created by backup_emc will be stored in $HOME/EMC_Backup

Backup archives are named like EMC_BACKUP_2026-03-01_12-38.tar.gz
and contain the archives EMC_CONFIG.tar.gz and EMC_FONTS.tar.gz and
can be restored whith the restore_emc.sh utility.

Install archives are named EMC_INSTALL.tar.gz; creating a new install archive will overwrite an existing one.
The content is stored in EMC_install archive directory.
How to use the install archive lookup README_INSTALL

To exclude directories or files from an install archive you can edit the
polybar_EXCLUDE_DIRS and polybar_EXCLUDE_FILES arrays in backup_emc.sh:

	polybar_EXCLUDE_DIRS=(x11 github install/setup)
	polybar_EXCLUDE_FILES=(bak old sav)

To RESTORE a backup archive call restore_emc.sh
restore_emc.sh works only with an archive created by backup_emc.
Other archives will not be processed.

